course: dictionary
lesson: 10783
title: Valleys and low points
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A valley is a low area of land between hills or mountains, often with a river running through it. The word is in the sentence «In the lumpy little valley the Mole trips and falls with a squeal.» The clues are lumpy, trips and falls, so the valley is a low, bumpy place, not a high one.
explain: Valley can also mean a low point between two high points, like on a graph or a wave. Look for clues such as high, low, or between. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it: a low point fits, but a high point would not make sense.
explain: Rivers and glaciers both make valleys, but slowly, over a very long time. A river carves a V-shaped valley, and a glacier carves a U-shaped one. When you learn a new word, ask what the sentences around it are telling you.
fact: A valley is a low area of land between hills or mountains.
fact: «Valley» can also mean a low point between two high points, like on a graph or a wave.
fact: Rivers carve V-shaped valleys over a very long time; glaciers carve U-shaped valleys.
fact: People often build towns and farms in valleys because the land is flat and there is water.
fact: Valleys can flood after heavy rain, and fog and cold air can collect there.
exercise: «In the lumpy little valley the Mole trips and falls with a squeal.» Where does the Mole fall? | On the top of a tall mountain | Under a bridge over a river | *In a low area of land between hills | In the middle of the sea
exercise: Mia says the valley on her graph is the highest point. What is a valley on a graph? | A point that is not on the graph | The highest point of the graph | *A low point between two high points | The line along the bottom edge of the paper
exercise: Which shape does a river usually carve into a valley? | *V-shaped | Round like a ball | Flat like a table | U-shaped
test: «About 700 years ago a wandering people settled in the Valley of Mexico.» What does valley mean in this sentence? | A very tall mountain | A big city with many tall buildings | A river that runs into the sea | *A low area of land between hills or mountains
test: Why do people often build towns and farms in valleys? | *Because the land is flat and there is water | Because valleys are too cold to live in | Because valleys are always high in the mountains | Because valleys never flood
exam: «A glacier carves deep valleys shaped like the letter U.» What shape does a glacier carve a valley into? | Circle | *U-shaped | Square | V-shaped
